  "final_text": "**Proposed disposition:** ESCALATE, confidence 0.7. The proposal is recorded as case C-A-261015-0003 and awaits a human decision.\n\n**Facts that drove it**\n1. The trader placed one SELL limit of 21,443, which is 8.17 times average top-5 depth. It sat 2 ticks from the touch and was one-sided. It had no fills and was fully cancelled.\n2. A 1,189 BUY market order executed 2.4 seconds after the SELL was placed. The whole SELL was cancelled 363 ms later. The discriminators show 3 repetitions in the session.\n3. No explanation holds up.\n   - The trader is a PROP trader with no registered market-making instruments.\n   - There were no market events and no risk events in the window.\n   - The order was not an iceberg and was not pegged.\n\n   Benefit is not clearly shown. Price move and reversion were both 0, and the BUY itself swept the ask from 9998 to 9999. I treated the evidence as mixed on that feature.\n\n**What would change my mind:** Evidence that the SELL was a genuine working order or a hedge for a parent order would move this toward closing. A clear favourable move with reversion on the other repeated cycles would move it toward DRAFT_STOR.",
